#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:115
msgid "Rule Precedence"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:117
msgid "From highest to lowest priority:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:119
msgid ""
"**Built-in security rules**: Hardcoded protections (e.g., `rm -rf /`). "
"Cannot be overridden."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:120
msgid "**`always_deny`**: Blocks matching actions"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:121
msgid "**`always_confirm`**: Requires confirmation for matching actions"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:122
msgid "**`always_allow`**: Auto-approves matching actions"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:123
msgid ""
"**Tool-specific `default`**: Per-tool fallback when no patterns match (e.g., "
"`tools.terminal.default`)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:124
msgid ""
"**Global `default`**: Falls back to `tool_permissions.default` when no tool-"
"specific default is set"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:126
msgid "Global Auto-Approve"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:128
msgid "To auto-approve all tool actions:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:140
msgid ""
"This bypasses confirmation prompts for most tools, but `always_deny`, "
"`always_confirm`, built-in security rules, and paths inside Zed settings "
"directories still prompt or block."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:142
msgid "Shell Compatibility"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:144
msgid ""
"For the `terminal` tool, Zed parses chained commands (e.g., `echo hello && "
"rm file`) to check each sub-command against your patterns."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:146
msgid ""
"All supported shells work with tool permission patterns, including sh, bash, "
"zsh, dash, fish, PowerShell 7+, pwsh, cmd, xonsh, csh, tcsh, Nushell, "
"Elvish, and rc (Plan 9)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:148
msgid "Writing Patterns"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:150
msgid ""
"Use `\\b` for word boundaries: `\\brm\\b` matches \"rm\" but not \"storm\""
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:151
msgid "Use `^` and `$` to anchor patterns to start/end of input"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:152
msgid "Escape special characters: `\\.` for literal dot, `\\\\` for backslash"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:156
msgid ""
"Test carefully—a typo in a deny pattern blocks legitimate actions. You can "
"use the \"Test Your Rules\" checker, available in each individual tool page, "
"to confirm whether a pattern is correctly falling in the desired condition."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:161
msgid "Built-in Security Rules"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:163
msgid ""
"Zed includes a small set of hardcoded security rules that **cannot be "
"overridden** by any setting. These only apply to the **terminal** tool and "
"block recursive deletion of critical directories:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:166
msgid "`rm -rf /` and `rm -rf /*` — filesystem root"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:167
msgid "`rm -rf ~` and `rm -rf ~/*` — home directory"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:168
msgid ""
"`rm -rf $HOME` / `rm -rf ${HOME}` (and `$HOME/*`) — home directory via "
"environment variable"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:169
msgid "`rm -rf .` and `rm -rf ./*` — current directory"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:170
msgid "`rm -rf ..` and `rm -rf ../*` — parent directory"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:172
msgid ""
"These patterns catch any flag combination (e.g., `-fr`, `-rfv`, `-r -f`, `--"
"recursive --force`) and are case-insensitive. They are checked against both "
"the raw command and each parsed sub-command in chained commands (e.g., `ls "
"&& rm -rf /`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:175
msgid ""
"There are no other built-in rules. The default settings file (<code "
"class=\"hljs\">zed: open default settings</code>) includes commented-out "
"examples for protecting `.env` files, secrets directories, and private keys "
"— you can uncomment or adapt these to suit your needs."
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:178
msgid "Permission Request in the UI"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:180
msgid ""
"When the agent requests permission, you'll see in the thread view a tool "
"card with a menu that includes:"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:182
msgid "**Allow once** / **Deny once** — One-time decision"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:183
msgid "**Always for <tool>** — Sets a tool-level default to allow or deny"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:184
msgid ""
"**Always for <pattern>** — Adds an `always_allow` or `always_deny` pattern "
"(when a safe pattern can be extracted)"
msgstr ""

#: src/ai/tool-permissions.md:186
msgid ""
"Selecting \"Always for <tool>\" sets `tools.<tool>.default` to allow or "
"deny. When a pattern can be safely extracted, selecting \"Always for "
"<pattern>\" adds an `always_allow` or `always_deny` rule for that input. MCP "
"tools only support the tool-level option."
msgstr ""

